                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8d5f0ea-452e-38c9-85c6-4dfa0bf3331c",
                        "entry_id": "6a873677-3047-3416-a16b-5de4d6c1fb99",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to ridicule, to scoff"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c3f6197-ab37-4f7d-b79a-a97e7fcaa6d0",
                                "sense_id": "a8d5f0ea-452e-38c9-85c6-4dfa0bf3331c",
                                "text": "Москва́ насто́лько интересова́лась происходя́щим на све́те, что встава́ла носка́ми ту́фель на вы́ступы фунда́мента и засма́тривалась внутрь кварти́р, пока́ её не осме́ивали прохо́жие.",
                                "translation": "Moscow was so interested by all that was happening in the world that she stood on tiptoe on the ledges above the buildings’ foundations and gazed into people’s rooms until passers-by began to laugh at her.",
                                "english": "Moscow was so interested by all that was happening in the world that she stood on tiptoe on the ledges above the buildings’ foundations and gazed into people’s rooms until passers-by began to laugh at her."
                            }
                        ]
